# --avoid / --prefer match the process NAME (comm), capped at 15 chars.
# Two constraints shaped these regexes:
#   1. systemd expands $EARLYOOM_ARGS with word-splitting, so no spaces.
#   2. EnvironmentFile unquoting eats backslashes, so no escapes. Literal
#      parens are matched with a dot instead, e.g. .sd-pam. for (sd-pam).
# 2026-08-31: dbus-broker-lau, (sd-pam), xdg-*, dconf-service and at-spi* were
# added to --avoid after earlyoom killed the session dbus broker 6 times during
# a vitest OOM. Those are all ~3 MiB, so killing them frees nothing and takes
# the audio stack and portals down with it. vitest was added to --prefer since
# its workers were the actual 2.4 GiB each hogs.
# 2026-09-29: steamwebhelper moved from --prefer to --avoid. During a rustc
# build OOM, earlyoom killed it about 68 times in one minute. Steam respawns it
# at once, so each kill freed nothing and flashed Steam windows over the screen.
# Compiler jobs (rustc, cc1plus, ld, mold, clang) are now preferred, since
# they are the actual multi-GiB hogs and a failed build is cheap to rerun.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 10,5 -s 100,100 -r 60 -p --avoid ^(systemd|systemd-.*|Hyprland|sshd|dbus-daemon|dbus-broker.*|.sd-pam.|xdg-.*|dconf-service|at-spi.*|pipewire|wireplumber|tailscaled|uwsm|earlyoom|steam|steamwebhelper)$ --prefer ^(rustc|cc1|cc1plus|ld|ld.lld|lld|mold|clang.*|dota2|chrome|chromium|firefox|electron|.*vitest.*)$"
